<title>UK: ICCO lists buffer stock cocoa for sale in August.</title>
<headline>ICCO lists buffer stock cocoa for sale in August.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The buffer stock manager of the International  Cocoa Organization (ICCO) said on Friday the buffer stock sales planned  for August would total a maximum 4,250 tonnes and would comprise the  following cocoa.</p>
<p>The date of the sale has yet to be announced.</p>
<p>Details of the cocoa offered for sale are as follows.</p>
<p> ORIGIN	  CROP YEAR     PORT	 TONNES	QUALITY</p>
<p> Ivory Coast    1987/88	Amsterdam    404	  GF</p>
<p> Ivory Coast    1987/88	Amsterdam  1,072	  FF</p>
<p> Togo	     1987/88	Amsterdam     49	  GF</p>
<p> Ghana	    1986/87	Amsterdam     95	  GF</p>
<p> Ghana	    1986/87	Amsterdam    100	  FF</p>
<p> Ghana	    1987/88	Amsterdam    795	  GF</p>
<p> Ghana	    1987/88	Amsterdam    497	  FF</p>
<p> Malaysia	 1987/88	Amsterdam    296	  GF</p>
<p> Malaysia	 1987/88	Amsterdam    296	  FF</p>
<p> Nigeria	  1986/87	Amsterdam     50	  GF</p>
<p> Nigeria	  1987/88	Amsterdam    298	  GF</p>
<p> Nigeria	  1987/88	Amsterdam    298	  FF</p>
<p>(FF=fairly fermented; GF=good fermented)</p>
<p>--Jalil Hamid, London Newsroom 44 71 542 4985</p>
